<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">British Kaffraria</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1847–1866</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">British Kaffraria was a British territory between the Keiskamma and Kei rivers in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-cape">Eastern Cape</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a>, annexed by Governor Sir Harry Smith in 1847 after the War of the Axe. Governed from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/king-williams-town">King William's Town</a> and made a separate crown colony in 1860, it was settled by Xhosa under British control and by German military settlers, and it was annexed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-colony">Cape Colony</a> in 1866.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/british-kaffraria.jpg" alt="British Kaffraria" width="320" height="280" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: I created the map, based partly on the source map: Eastern frontier of the Colony of the Cape of Good Hope from Algoa... · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Eastern_Frontier,_Cape_of_Good_Hope,_ca_1835.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
